        <mj-text font-weight="bold" font-size="20px" color="#005C84" font-family="Roboto">Greetings from Digital Preservation Southampton</mj-text>

      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <!-- Welcome -->
    <mj-section padding="0px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text font-family="Roboto" align=left>
          We hope you are doing very well. Greetings to our new subscribers since our last message. The DPS mailing list is a space to hear about upcoming events, news, and stories from our team. As we leave the summer behind us, the DPS team is ready to take on a new academic year. We have got some exciting new training offers planned. Here are some of our latest news and events. 
        </mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <!-- Welcome Image -->
    <mj-section>
      <mj-column>
        <mj-image src="https://images.pexels.com/photos/331684/pexels-photo-331684.jpeg" alt="Photo of computer" width="593px" height="200px"/>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <!-- Upcoming Events -->
    <mj-section padding="10px 20px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text font-size="20px" font-family="Roboto" font-weight="bold">Upcoming Workshop</mj-text>

        <!-- Workshop 1 -->
        
        <mj-text font-family="Roboto" font-size="16px" font-weight="bold" padding-top="16px">Foundations of Digital Preservation: Integrity Checking, Format Migration, and Workflows (Online)</mj-text>
        <mj-text font-family="Roboto">
          Following the success of our Mastering Metadata workshops, we are launching a new exciting workshop. This is your digital preservation essentials course; a hands-on, online workshop designed to introduce the core concepts, tools, and workflows related to the preservation of digital assets. Learn to identify and migrate file formats, create safe data transfers, and ensure long-term access through integrity checks. Through this workshop, you will earn experience with key open-source and industry-standard software such as DROID, Siegfried, Teracopy, and standards such as BagIt. Registrations are open. Do not miss your chance! 
          <br /><br />
          <strong>October 17, 2025</strong><br />
          12pm-4:30pm BST (<a href="https://www.timeanddate.com/worldclock/converter.html?iso=20251017T114500&p1=136">See in your timezone</a>)<br />
          Location: Online<br />
          <a href="https://store.southampton.ac.uk/short-courses/faculty-of-arts-and-humanities/digital-preservation-advisory-unit/foundations-of-digital-preservation-integrity-checking-format-migration-and-workflows-online">Register Here</a>
          <br /><br />
          <strong>Are there discounted places available?</strong> 
          <br /><br />
          Yes, we are able to evaluate cases for discounted places, particularly for participants from <a href="https://www.oecd.org/en/topics/oda-eligibility-and-conditions/dac-list-of-oda-recipients.html">Official Development Assistance (ODA)</a> countries. Please email us describing your situation and we will offer you a discounted ticket. 
        </mj-text>
        <mj-image src="https://media.licdn.com/dms/image/v2/D4D22AQGrrvWla6PSxw/feedshare-shrink_800/B4DZk0JzoMH0Ak-/0/1757516610880?e=1760572800&v=beta&t=TyiZ34GbU2N9Qy5VlV02uV4TGBxmxFykh8ZkW2TCIlA" width="593px" />
        
        
        <!-- Upcoming Workshops Table -->
        <mj-text font-size="16px" font-family="Roboto" font-weight="bold">Other Upcoming Workshops</mj-text>
        <mj-text font-family="Roboto">
        Below, you will find our current plan for upcoming workshops for the remainder of the year. We will promptly notify you once registrations open and dates are solidified. 
        </mj-text>
        <mj-table font-family="Roboto" font-size="14px" cellpadding="10px" cellspacing="0" width="100%">
          <tr style="background-color:#d9dce1; font-weight:bold;">
            <th align="left">Workshop</th>
            <th align="left">Date</th>
            <th align="left" style="white-space: nowrap;">Format</th>
          </tr>
